      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need mkFileObj to be scoped but not err.  You can\u0027t define two variables with different scopes using :\u003d, and you need err to be declared when you call if, so you\u0027d have to introduce an extra scope between declaring mkFileObj and err:\n\n    var mkFileObj *os.File\n    {\n        var err error\n        mkFileObj, err \u003d logger.CreateFileWithRotation(mkFile, 1)\n        if err !\u003d nil {\n            return nil\n        }\n    }\n\nThat doesn\u0027t seem worth it.",
